.TH TDE\-FIREWALLD\-TRAY 1 "November 2026" "tde-firewalld 0.1.0" "Trinity Desktop Environment"
.SH NAME
tde\-firewalld\-tray \- system tray icon for the firewalld firewall
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tde\-firewalld\-tray
.RI [ "generic TDE and TQt options" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tde\-firewalld\-tray
shows the state of
.BR firewalld (1)
as an icon in the system tray of the Trinity panel (kicker). The tooltip
shows the default zone and the active zones. The icon is greyed out when
firewalld is not running and shows a red stop sign while panic mode is on.
.PP
A left click opens the Firewall Manager,
.BR tde\-firewalld (1).
The context menu changes the default zone, turns panic mode on or off,
reloads the firewall, and enables or disables starting the icon at login.
.PP
Only one instance runs per session; starting it again does nothing.
.SH AUTOSTART
The icon is
.B not
started automatically by default. TDE starts it at login only when
.B Start Automatically at Login
is checked in its menu, which sets
.B Autostart=true
in the
.B [General]
group of
.IR tde\-firewalld\-trayrc .
.SH AUTHENTICATION
Showing the icon only uses firewalld requests covered by the
.I org.fedoraproject.FirewallD1.info
polkit action, which every user may use, so it never asks for a password
on its own. Changing the default zone, panic mode or reloading the firewall
asks for authentication through the session's polkit agent
.RB ( polkit\-agent\-tde ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.trinity/share/config/tde\-firewalld\-trayrc
Per-user settings ([General] Autostart).
.TP
.I /opt/trinity/share/autostart/tde\-firewalld\-tray\-autostart.desktop
Session autostart entry, guarded by
.BR X\-TDE\-autostart\-condition=tde\-firewalld\-trayrc:General:Autostart:false .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tde\-firewalld (1),
.BR firewalld (1),
.BR firewall\-cmd (1),
.BR polkit (8)
.PP
The handbook is available in the TDE Help Center
.RI ( help:/tde\-firewalld/tray.html ).
